# Platform custom domains & SSL (P2-D)

Super Admin **Domains** tab is the single pane for CNAME verification, SSL lifecycle, and expiry KPIs. Denali workspace packages are **not** modified — ingress resolves tenant via platform subdomain parse or verified custom hostname only.

## Data model

`tenant_domains` gains SSL columns (migration `20260621140000_tenant_domains_ssl`):

| Column | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `ssl_status` | `pending` → `provisioning` → `active` \| `failed` |
| `ssl_expires_at` | Cert expiry (stub: +90d) |
| `ssl_last_error` | Provider failure message |
| `last_observed_cname` | Internal — not exposed in DTO v1 |

`status` (CNAME) semantics unchanged: `pending` → `verified`.

**UI “Expired”:** derived when `sslStatus === "active"` and `sslExpiresAt < now()` — no DB value `expired`.

## Verify + SSL flow

```text
POST /platform/v1/tenants/{id}/domains/{domainId}/verify
  → verifyTenantDomainCnameLive(hostname, cnameTarget)
  → 422 { ok: false, message } on CNAME mismatch
  → markVerified(domainId, lastObservedCname)
  → audit DOMAIN_VERIFIED (outside transaction)
  → provisionTenantDomainSsl → stub|cloudflare provider
  → audit DOMAIN_SSL_PROVISIONED | DOMAIN_SSL_FAILED
  → 200 { ok: true, domain: TenantDomainDto }
```

## Public ingress (custom host)

```text
GET /public/tenant-context  Host: www.custom.example.com
  → resolvePublicIngressSubdomain(host)
       1) resolveSubdomainFromPlatformHost (tenant-kernel parse)
       2) else resolveTenantFromCustomDomainHost (verified + ssl active)
  → resolvePublicTenantContextBySubdomain (unchanged)
```

Surfaces v1: **`marketing`** · **`portal`** only — no admin custom host.

## API

| Method | Path | RBAC |
|--------|------|------|
| GET | `/platform/v1/tenants/{id}/domains` | ops auth — DTO includes SSL fields |
| POST | `/platform/v1/tenants/{id}/domains/{domainId}/verify` | write — live DNS + SSL provision |
| GET | `/platform/v1/domains/ssl-summary` | ops auth (all roles) |
| POST | `/platform/v1/domains/run-ssl-expiry-check` | owner only |

### ssl-summary response

```json
{ "expiringWithin14Days": 0 }
```

### run-ssl-expiry-check response

```json
{ "expiring": ["www.example.com"], "audited": 1 }
```

Audits `DOMAIN_SSL_EXPIRING` per hostname in the 14-day window.

## Environment

| Variable | Values | When |
|----------|--------|------|
| `PLATFORM_DOMAIN_VERIFY_STUB` | `pass` | Dev/test — CNAME verify always ok without observed match |
| `PLATFORM_DOMAIN_DNS_LOOKUP` | `live` (default) \| `off` | `off` → lookup returns null |
| `PLATFORM_SSL_PROVIDER` | `stub` (default) \| `cloudflare` | Factory in `create-platform-ssl-provider.ts` |
| `PLATFORM_SSL_CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | secret | Required for cloudflare success path |

## Audit actions

| Action | When |
|--------|------|
| `DOMAIN_VERIFIED` | CNAME verify success |
| `DOMAIN_SSL_PROVISIONED` | SSL active |
| `DOMAIN_SSL_FAILED` | SSL provisioning failed |
| `DOMAIN_SSL_EXPIRING` | Manual expiry check (14d window) |

Platform routes append audit via `appendPlatformAuditEventOutsideTx` (no surrounding tenant transaction).

## UI

- Club detail **Domains** tab: `data-ssl-status` badge per row (`domainSslDisplayBadge`)
- Overview KPI: `data-stat-ssl-expiring` (14-day window from ssl-summary BFF)

## Key modules

| Module | Path |
|--------|------|
| Live DNS | `lookup-tenant-domain-cname.ts` |
| Verify | `verify-tenant-domain.ts` (`verifyTenantDomainCnameLive`) |
| SSL providers | `platform/ssl/create-platform-ssl-provider.ts` |
| Provision | `provision-tenant-domain-ssl.ts` |
| Custom ingress | `resolve-public-ingress-subdomain.ts` |

